- entry .sized   `xs.sized[n]`: checks a value's length once, recording it as `& Sized[n]`
-     `Array(1, 2, 3, 4).sized[4]` is `Optional[xs.type & Sized[4]]`: `Unset` when the length
-     differs, and otherwise the value with its length in its type, so a literal ordinal below
-     `n` reads bare and one at or beyond it does not compile. The counterpart of `occupied` for
-     length, for any `Countable` value; the literal constructors `Array.fill(n)`, `Array.tabulate
-     (n)` and `Data.fill(n)` brand their results the same way when `n` is a literal (a `val`
-     length does not). Shipping in the `concordance` library.
